<script>
  import CauseTable from '#lib/kb/CauseTable.svelte';
  import Callout from '#lib/kb/Callout.svelte';
  import RenderStamp from '#lib/kb/RenderStamp.svelte';
  import reports from '#lib/data/reports-4471.json';
  import notes from '#lib/data/desk-notes.json';
  import { groupByCause, readAs, uniqueById } from '#lib/kb/causes';
  import { tenantOf } from '#lib/kb/locales';
  const signature = 'v1.eyJzdWIiOiIyMDc3IiwiYXVkIjoiY2hhbGxlbmdlOndoYXQtaXQtc2hvd3MiLCJpYXQiOjE3OTM0MDAyOTYsImV4cCI6MTc5MzQ4NjY5Nn0.iNfi1KMdB7DrgD-djT0AnhsIsjLAXKEpWagPz3fGe40';

  const merged = uniqueById(reports).filter((r) => r.mergedInto === 4471);
  const groups = groupByCause(merged, tenantOf);
  const by = (c) => groups.find((g) => g.cause === c);
  const parser = by('parser'), hint = by('hint');
  const oneDay = readAs(parser, notes.oneDayMove);
  const dupes = reports.length - merged.length;
  const retagged = (g, tag) => g.taggedAs[tag] ?? 0;
</script>

[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged **{merged.length} reports** as one issue and marked it known. Read by
tenant (locale and booking form), not by intake tag, they are two problems.

<Callout>
Not one issue. One fix queued covers only the larger of two.
</Callout>

## The two problems

| Problem | Reports | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| `parser` | {parser.reports.length} | The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get flipped dates. Affects {parser.tenants} tenants. |
| `hint` | {hint.reports.length} | `booking-v3` prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so day-first people type month first. A form bug, not a parser bug. Affects alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour. |

{parser.reports.length} + {hint.reports.length} = {merged.length}. {oneDay} of the {parser.reports.length} (R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) are one-day moves, not month flips: likely a time zone bug. The desk files them under `parser` by tenant and footnotes them there.

## What the counts rest on

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

- The export repeats {dupes} reports across overlapping pages. One id is one report.
- Intake tags are wrong for {retagged(parser, 'hint') + retagged(hint, 'parser')} reports: {retagged(parser, 'hint')} tagged `hint` are `parser`, {retagged(hint, 'parser')} tagged `parser` are `hint`.
  Only the tenant's locale and form say which.

## What changed

The desk now merges on cause, not subject: [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause)
replaces 0001, and the [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) follows it. Tickets: #1 (`parser`, {parser.reports.length}),
#2 (`hint`, {hint.reports.length}), both closed by pull request #4.

## Lessons

- Merging on subject alone (decision 0001) hid a second problem inside one count.
- A fix for the parser will not fix `booking-v3`.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
